WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.610
Start in the Congo rainforest.

2
00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:07.770
Rainforests get between 2,000 and
10,000 millimetres of rain a year.

3
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.130
Head north, and the forest
gives way to savanna:

4
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:14.190
grassland with a wet
season and a dry season.

5
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.630
Keep going, into the Sahara.

6
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.190
Hot deserts get about
250 millimetres a year.

7
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.030
And it isn't just Africa.

8
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.850
Around the world, biomes form
rough bands across the map.

9
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.690
So why do the world's big
ecosystems come in bands?

10
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.370
Is the desert just too far from the sea?

11
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.930
In this mission, you'll
map the world's biomes,

12
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.430
from rainforest to tundra.

13
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:42.290
Then you'll read climate graphs, and match
each biome to its rain and temperature.

14
00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.520
Your mission: explain why the
world's biomes line up in bands.
